=== Scenario 14 (FABRIC TEST-NETWORK): RecallCampaigns, the one-to-many
=== replacement for the pre-v3.5 scalar RecallBatchID/Reason/ReasonHistory
=== fields, version 3.5, sequence 10. Produced by
=== scripts/scenario_14_recall_campaigns_live.sh against the same
=== three-organisation Fabric test-network used throughout this
=== dissertation. Unedited console output below (ANSI colour codes
=== stripped only).
===
=== This scenario closes the gap named explicitly in supervisor review of
=== the fifth draft and, until this version, deliberately documented as a
=== partial solution: the RecallBatchID fix evaluated through v3.4
=== (Scenario 7) prevented one recall campaign from silently overwriting
=== another, but a second, independent campaign against the same product
=== could only ever be reported as skippedOverlap -- it was never itself
=== tracked or independently resolvable. PRODUCT-OV14 is assembled from
=== two components in two different batches, then recalled under BOTH:
=== Part A shows both BATCH-OV14-X and BATCH-OV14-Y open simultaneously in
=== recallCampaigns, something no pre-v3.5 GetComponent response could
=== ever show. Part B shows CloseRecall resolving BATCH-OV14-X's campaign
=== alone (to REPAIRED) while BATCH-OV14-Y stays RECALLED and the
=== product's overall recallStatus stays RECALLED, then RevokeRecall
=== clearing BATCH-OV14-Y; both campaigns' full history (reason,
=== reasonHistory, terminal status) remains on the ledger afterwards,
=== rather than being deleted the way the pre-v3.5 scalar fields were on
=== revocation.

